# An ingredient, scaled and in the cook's units
// Its amount is for the recipe's own number of people:  shown for how many are eating, in metric or in cups and spoons.
// A box beside it picks it for the shopping list.

an ingredient
	its "scaled amount" is its amount * the scale of recipe cards
		// For how many are eating:  its amount times diners over servings
	its "shown" is
		// Its scaled amount in the cook's units
		set scaled to its scaled amount
		if the units of recipe cards is cups
			if its unit is "g" and its grams per cup > 0 return measure (scaled / its grams per cup) in quarters of "cups"
			if its unit is "g" return measure (scaled / (1 oz in g)) in "oz"
			if its unit is "kg" return measure (scaled * 1000 / (1 oz in g)) in "oz"
			if its unit is "ml" return measure scaled in spoons or cups
			if its unit is "l" return measure (scaled * 1000) in spoons or cups
		otherwise
			if its unit is "cups" and its grams per cup > 0 return measure (scaled * its grams per cup) in "g"
			if its unit is "cups" return measure (scaled * (1 cup in ml)) in "ml"
			if its unit is "oz" return measure (scaled * (1 oz in g)) in "g"
			if its unit is "lb" return measure (scaled * (1 lb in g)) in "g"
		if its unit is "cups" or its unit is "tbsp" or its unit is "tsp"
			return measure scaled in quarters of its unit
		return measure scaled in its unit

	to draw it
		// A box to pick it, how much, and what
		<form value={it}>
			<stack direction="horizontal" spacing="sm" class="ingredient">
				<checkbox name="picked" aria-label="Tick to add to the shopping list" />
				<text bold class="how-much">{the written of its shown}</text>
				<text>{its name}</text>
			</stack>
		</form>
